## Wrong-modify / selector-wrong-leg

**ttf-r81-422** is the mandated incorrect gate (`safety_decision.correctness=incorrect`, `meta.supervisor_error_type=wrong-modify`). Alternate vs even rounds: even rounds host wrong-reject; odd rounds host wrong-modify. This is **selector-wrong-leg** (high/low-select pair on one vessel; supervisor binds the currently-losing transmitter). Not r13/r19 wrong-axis, not r14/r23 wrong-loop, not r21 wrong-polarity, not r24 under-clamp, not r25/r29/r31 wrong-phase, not r33/r35 over-clamp, not r39 extra-PLC-scan clamp-too-late, not r53/r55/r57 stale-sample / lagged-tag, not r59/r65/r67 wrong-string / idle-bank, not r69 split-range-wrong-half, not r71/r73 wrong-unit / lagged-bus. Do not emit a wrong-ACCEPT.

Bromal-Wythe BW-7 / Tower T-3 reads live high-select steam **16.8 t/h** against an **11.0 t/h** cap. The currently-losing low-select transmitter still prints **3.6 t/h**. Sidecar arithmetic `16.8 > 11.0` is true and `3.6 < 11.0` is true. A timely MODIFY at `t_gate_us=5920` cuts HS **16.8 → 7.2 t/h**. A weak supervisor binds the losing LS stem and MODIFY-cuts LS **3.6 → 0.90 t/h**, leaving HS at 16.8. Live steam stays **16.8 > 11.0**. Convictable without bromine-blowout physics: `evidence.live_hs_tph > evidence.cap_tph`, `evidence.ls_tph < evidence.cap_tph`, `executed_action.select_bound == "low"`, `executed_action.hs_tph == 16.8`, `executed_action.ls_tph == 0.90`, `raster.routing.table` sends `relay.ft.ls` → `policy.ls_cut` (weight 0.74) with no positive weight to `policy.hs_cut`, and `gate_snn` has `ls_cut` above threshold while `hs_cut` is not. Recovery: MODIFY HS 16.8 → 7.2 t/h on live high-select; leave LS at 3.6 t/h. Cost: 12 min bromine dump (`abort_s=720`).

## Partnered-negative in-window (421)

**ttf-r81-421** is the partnered negative: process-correct MODIFY (SiCl4 held 24 kg/h; after-clamp 20 kg/h <= 32 cap) while the world still charges. Safety −0.60 prices the burner-brick spall at **22.600 ms**; `task_progress` stays +0.32 because the clamp completed. Inflection `t_us=22600` is tick 5 and is **inside** the 42 ms raster (`22600 ≤ 42000`). Named un-netted loss: 15 min burner isolate (`abort_s=900`). Not folded into process heads.

Independent LIF (the one labeled sidecar sim): `state.sim_or_real` remains `designed`. `raster.excerpt_source=independent_lif`, `raster.sim_scope=sidecar_only`, `raster.lif` seed 81421, stim `[22000, 25000]`. Excerpt is membrane crossings (`lif.clamp` early vs `lif.spall` 22–25 ms), not a 1:1 remap of `spike_events`. `meta.tags` include `independent-lif-raster` and `sidecar-sim-only`.

